commit 487d9abe8dee1749be9919d4555e4bb61afd8d21
Author: Jack Shelton <me@jackshelton.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 12 01:05:27 2026 -0500

    feat: tiny-translator measured journey corrections; silent-data-loss red found

    Measured and landed: filter radios were never actually clicked (host
    stretches full width, clicks landed in empty space and silently
    selected nothing — label-targeted now); reviewer-half semantics (the
    committed unit LEAVES the Review-needed filter; final state reads back
    under All units); download capture polled to declared expectations;
    the editor commit anchored on the app's own settled reaction (undo
    losing disabled) never a sleep — and that anchor is what turned silent
    data loss into a hard red: the migrated lane's debounced
    valueChanges→propagateChange never reaches the outer control while the
    era lane fires in ~200ms; the exported XLIFF carries state=final with
    the ORIGINAL text. Nothing published over it. Root-cause unit next —
    the pipe translation was our own capability's output. 1933/1933.

